      "lang": "en",
      "title": "Euro area inflation: headline seen steady near 3.8% into year-end",
      "body": "We forecast euro area headline HICP inflation at 3.8% y/y in December 2026, broadly unchanged from the 3.8% published for September and 1.77 pp above the ECB's 2% target. A favourable base effect of -0.11 pp is offset by forecast price momentum of 0.12 pp. Services (1.52 pp) and fuels (1.30 pp) are the largest contributors to the December rate, with fuel prices up 32.3% y/y.\n\nThe distribution around the central forecast is wide. We estimate a 95% probability that December inflation exceeds 3%, 79% that it exceeds 3.5%, 27% that it exceeds 4% and 7% that it exceeds 5%. The 90% band spans 3.0% to 5.1%.\n\nAt the three-month horizon, the model's RMSE of 0.63 pp compares with 0.80 pp for a random walk. The main limitation is performance in shock periods: in 2020-2023 only 35.4% of outcomes fell inside the 68% band, and the model under-predicted inflation by 0.37 pp on average.",
